WEBVTT

1
00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:43.160
Zachary. what you doing?

2
00:02:44.498 --> 00:02:46.160
The drawers stick.

3
00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:47.827
Not for me. they didn't.

4
00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.792
Morning. Ruby.

5
00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.903
- Sticky drawers.
- Okay.

6
00:02:54.241 --> 00:02:56.472
- Um. you missed a call.
- Who?

7
00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.503
- Ten minutes ago.
- Thanks.

8
00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:02.807
Ruby. Who was it?

9
00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:05.384
- Hmm?
- Who was it?

10
00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.215
None of your business.

11
00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.627
This is Deputy Moretti.

12
00:03:16.096 --> 00:03:19.396
<i>Hey. it's good to hear your
voice. What's going on?</i>

13
00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.800
Work.

14
00:03:21.001 --> 00:03:24.062
Yeah. me. too. Actually.
that's why I'm calling.

15
00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:27.969
Looks like your department
put a flag on a Will Balint.

16
00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.365
Name ring a bell?

17
00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:33.604
- Yeah. it does. Why? What'd he do?
- He died.

18
00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.195
<i>Sheriff Wilkins
isn't at the office.</i>

19
00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:41.259
<i>He's already headed to the
Cumberland County morgue.</i>

20
00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:42.789
Tell him we'll meet him there.

21
00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.390
We'll meet him there.

22
00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.320
<i>So. what brings you
to Cumberland County?</i>

23
00:03:49.396 --> 00:03:50.396
This guy.

24
00:03:50.564 --> 00:03:51.564
<i>Oh.</i>

25
00:03:51.732 --> 00:03:54.827
I called them. Sheriff. I had
to because they never call me.

26
00:03:55.869 --> 00:03:57.337
So. how'd he die?

27
00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.404
Oil rig accident.

28
00:04:01.108 --> 00:04:02.804
<i>Overhead pipe slid
loose from its chain.</i>

29
00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:05.275
struck him in the back of
the head. knocking him out.

30
00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:08.005
He fell face-first into
some mud. suffocated.

31
00:04:08.215 --> 00:04:10.548
- How deep was the mud?
- Three inches.

32
00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.149
Seriously?

33
00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:13.730
Well. if you're unconscious.

34
00:04:13.754 --> 00:04:16.053
that's plenty deep to
block your air passage.

35
00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:17.647
Yeah.

36
00:04:18.859 --> 00:04:20.987
- Anyone see this happen?
<i>- No.</i>

37
00:04:21.895 --> 00:04:24.888
They didn't even find the guy until
one of the next fellas came on shift.

38
00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.293
By then. it was too late.

39
00:04:27.134 --> 00:04:30.332
What makes you so damned
interested in him anyway?

40
00:04:30.971 --> 00:04:34.032
Will Balint is a suspect
in a recent rape case.

41
00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.743
Seems suspicious he
now shows up dead.

42
00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:40.546
Well. hell. he's
an oil rigger. Walt.

43
00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:43.478
Newett Energy's actually got a
better safety record than most.

44
00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:47.109
But with that drill turning 24/7.
there's bound to be accidents.

45
00:04:47.888 --> 00:04:51.256
Remind me. Jim. you still
owe me a favor or is it my turn?

46
00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:54.553
I lent you Eamonn. so I reckon
the next favor comes from you.

47
00:04:54.928 --> 00:04:57.159
Might have to make it two. then.

48
00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.822
Would you mind if I looked
around that oil rig a bit?

49
00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.165
It's not your county. Walt.

50
00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:04.433
I know that.

51
00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:08.371
But if this death is a result of
something that happened in my county.

52
00:05:08.542 --> 00:05:11.171
I can't help but feel
some responsibility here.

53
00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:14.979
All right. You go
take your look.

54
00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:18.714
But I'm sending Deputy
O'Neill here along as an escort.

55
00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.181
<i>I know how you get. Walt.</i>

56
00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:24.415
I don't want you forgetting that oil
company provides a lot of revenue

57
00:05:24.591 --> 00:05:26.492
and a lot of jobs
in this county.

58
00:05:28.395 --> 00:05:29.635
<i>Will was a good worker.</i>

59
00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.990
Hell. he was better than
good. He was outstanding.

60
00:05:32.132 --> 00:05:35.296
That's why I just promoted
him to assistant driller.

61
00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:38.561
- What was Will's previous position?
- Roughneck.

62
00:05:39.573 --> 00:05:42.018
Are those the guys whose job it
is to physically force young girls

63
00:05:42.042 --> 00:05:43.305
into having sexual intercourse?

64
00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.774
Those charges were dropped.

65
00:05:44.945 --> 00:05:49.280
Or does "innocent until proven guilty"
only hold true in Cumberland County?

66
00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:52.044
Walker. we're all just
trying to do our jobs here.

67
00:05:52.219 --> 00:05:55.155
And our friends from Absaroka are
here with Sheriff Wilkins' blessing.

68
00:05:55.322 --> 00:05:58.952
So. I need you to be as forthcoming
with them as you were with us.

69
00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:01.024
Of course. My apologies.

70
00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:04.961
It's just a little unsettling
to lose one of your own.

71
00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:08.029
You know how that
is. don't you. Sheriff?

72
00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:12.335
- Who found the body?
<i>- Trot Simic.</i>

73
00:06:12.806 --> 00:06:15.640
Trot! Get up here. tell
them what you know.

74
00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:27.985
Yeah. I clocked in. then I
walked up here to start my shift.

75
00:06:28.555 --> 00:06:30.581
And I saw Will
laying in the mud.

76
00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:32.919
- Was he dead when you found him?
- Yeah.

77
00:06:34.094 --> 00:06:36.359
I mean. I tried to clear
his airway and do CPR.

78
00:06:36.897 --> 00:06:38.798
<i>You know. just in case.</i>

79
00:06:39.099 --> 00:06:41.762
But I couldn't remember how
many breaths for each push.

80
00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:46.396
There ain't nothing you could do.
Don't beat yourself up on this one.

81
00:06:46.907 --> 00:06:48.102
Yeah.

82
00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.373
Where did this
accident happen. Trot?

83
00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:53.463
Trot found Will right down there.
a 30-foot pipe right beside him.

84
00:06:54.014 --> 00:06:57.178
I don't know if he got hit down there
or if he got knocked off the platform.

85
00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.251
So. you just tossed
Will Balint's body aside

86
00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:00.979
so you all could just
get back to work?

87
00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:04.089
Look. everybody knows
what they're getting into here.

88
00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:07.591
It's a dangerous job. People get
hurt. That's why it pays what it pays.

89
00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:10.706
<i>But if we were to stop production
every time there was an on-site accident.</i>

90
00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:11.891
however sad.

91
00:07:12.065 --> 00:07:15.558
we'd immediately start hemorrhaging
hundreds of thousands of dollars.

92
00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.666
<i>We'd all be out of a job.</i>

93
00:07:18.238 --> 00:07:19.238
Speaking of which...

94
00:07:19.406 --> 00:07:22.342
That's enough gossip.
boys! Go on. get back to work!

95
00:07:43.496 --> 00:07:46.042
Just so you know. we did document
the scene and take statements

96
00:07:46.066 --> 00:07:49.764
before Sheriff Wilkins gave the okay
for production to start back up again.

97
00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:53.031
So you think it was an accident?
- I do.

98
00:07:53.807 --> 00:07:55.639
Clearly. you don't.

99
00:07:55.809 --> 00:07:58.301
What is it. just the
coincidence of the timing?

100
00:07:58.478 --> 00:08:00.538
Walt doesn't believe
in coincidence.

101
00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.681
There's also the
matter of that promotion.

102
00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:06.750
Well. sure. A guy's new at his job.
he's more likely to make a mistake.

103
00:08:06.987 --> 00:08:08.497
Especially if he
leapfrogs all the way up

104
00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:10.615
from roughneck to
assistant driller in one day.

105
00:08:10.991 --> 00:08:12.015
Is that weird?

106
00:08:12.359 --> 00:08:16.524
Me and Henry spent most of our
20s working rigs up in Prudhoe Bay.

107
00:08:16.696 --> 00:08:20.098
All those years. I never saw anybody
get made up from roughneck to AD

108
00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:22.547
without being a derrickman
for at least a couple of years.

109
00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:25.797
So what's so special about Will
Balint to make him the exception?

110
00:08:29.576 --> 00:08:31.936
Well. let me take a look
at these guys' work records

111
00:08:32.045 --> 00:08:33.479
and performance reviews.

112
00:08:33.646 --> 00:08:34.841
That might explain things.

113
00:08:35.148 --> 00:08:36.348
How are you gonna manage that?

114
00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:39.315
I'll just tell them they can comply
with Cumberland's modest request

115
00:08:39.486 --> 00:08:42.251
or I'll sic these two
Absaroka hard-asses on them.

116
00:09:03.376 --> 00:09:04.537
Henry?

117
00:09:07.981 --> 00:09:09.381
Hello. Cady.

118
00:09:10.283 --> 00:09:13.082
- You look nice.
- Thank you. You don't.

119
00:09:15.655 --> 00:09:16.782
Car trouble.

120
00:09:19.059 --> 00:09:20.152
So. what is the occasion?

121
00:09:20.326 --> 00:09:21.487
<i>I'm going to meet a client</i>

122
00:09:21.661 --> 00:09:23.630
from one of the case
files that Mathias gave me.

123
00:09:23.797 --> 00:09:25.517
Someone set fire to
Collin Burnside's house.

124
00:09:25.632 --> 00:09:28.033
so I'm trying to push the
feds to open an investigation.

125
00:09:29.636 --> 00:09:31.628
- Knock 'em dead.
- Thanks.

126
00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:45.609
<i>Wait. so. what
happened to Gab's rapist?</i>

127
00:09:46.086 --> 00:09:48.282
He got promoted. And
then he got knocked out

128
00:09:48.455 --> 00:09:51.323
in a work-related accident and
suffocated in three inches of mud.

129
00:09:51.958 --> 00:09:52.958
Wow!

130
00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:55.054
Some coincidence.

131
00:09:55.695 --> 00:09:59.188
You think someone was trying
to get revenge for Gab's rape?

132
00:09:59.466 --> 00:10:01.298
If there was. we
need to figure out

133
00:10:01.468 --> 00:10:04.461
who knew enough to even
identify Will Balint as a rapist.

134
00:10:05.138 --> 00:10:07.107
Well. there's Gab. of course.

135
00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:09.333
- Her mom. Linda.
<i>- Yeah.</i>

136
00:10:09.509 --> 00:10:13.344
- May Stillwater and Gab's friend. Mandy.
- And us.

137
00:10:14.714 --> 00:10:15.958
We can't take anything
for granted. right?

138
00:10:15.982 --> 00:10:17.942
I mean. a badge and gun
doesn't make you flawless.

139
00:10:20.086 --> 00:10:21.884
- You're right.
- He is?

140
00:10:22.589 --> 00:10:23.589
<i>Malachi.</i>

141
00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:27.282
His badge didn't keep him from
being a corrupt tribal police chief.

142
00:10:27.494 --> 00:10:29.895
Malachi also knew
about Gab's rapists

143
00:10:30.096 --> 00:10:33.294
after Mathias and I took a look
at the casino's security footage.

144
00:10:33.466 --> 00:10:38.029
- Walt. You missed two more calls.
<i>- I'll have to try back later.</i>

145
00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:41.760
You know. it's also possible

146
00:10:41.841 --> 00:10:44.640
that this didn't have
anything to do with Gab's rape.

147
00:10:44.878 --> 00:10:47.848
Vic said that Will Balint
was just promoted. right?

148
00:10:48.081 --> 00:10:51.643
Maybe one of his co-workers
had a hard time with it.

149
00:10:51.818 --> 00:10:53.309
Professional jealousy. you know?

150
00:10:54.988 --> 00:10:56.957
Brings up hard feelings.

151
00:10:57.757 --> 00:10:59.157
That's true.

152
00:11:00.026 --> 00:11:04.396
Vic. I want you to drive back to Oden
and see if you can find Archer Loftus.

153
00:11:04.631 --> 00:11:06.065
Who's Archer Loftus?

154
00:11:06.232 --> 00:11:07.776
<i>He's a roughneck
I met at the casino.</i>

155
00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:11.259
He's a whistleblower.
a conspiracy theorist.

156
00:11:11.838 --> 00:11:16.276
If Ferg is right and this is about
internal politics at Newett Energy.

157
00:11:16.442 --> 00:11:18.035
Archer will know about it.

158
00:11:18.611 --> 00:11:19.704
Why do I have to go?

159
00:11:19.879 --> 00:11:22.576
- It was Ferg's theory.
- Well. if memory serves.

160
00:11:22.749 --> 00:11:25.218
you and Eamonn had the best
working relationship of any of us.

161
00:11:25.952 --> 00:11:28.387
Zach. Ferg. I want you
two to put together a list

162
00:11:28.555 --> 00:11:32.515
of all of Gab's close
family members and friends.

163
00:11:32.692 --> 00:11:35.890
Anybody that may have been
motivated to see her rapists punished.

164
00:11:36.062 --> 00:11:38.463
On it. How about you?

165
00:11:41.267 --> 00:11:43.532
I think someone
needs to talk to Gab.

166
00:11:43.703 --> 00:11:46.502
She deserves to know
that Will Balint is dead.

167
00:11:59.719 --> 00:12:00.846
Thanks for coming.

168
00:12:01.654 --> 00:12:04.488
I wanted you to be here
when Gab heard the news.

169
00:12:04.724 --> 00:12:07.558
- What news?
- One of her rapists was killed.

170
00:12:15.702 --> 00:12:18.262
<i>Thank you for talking with us.</i>

171
00:12:21.941 --> 00:12:23.876
Gab. is your mom at work?

172
00:12:24.911 --> 00:12:26.345
She quit last week.

173
00:12:27.547 --> 00:12:32.451
- What's she doing now?
- Taking a vacation. Somewhere.

174
00:12:34.621 --> 00:12:36.453
She bought this
TV before she left.

175
00:12:39.892 --> 00:12:43.329
- When's she coming back?
- Check the freezer.

176
00:12:52.205 --> 00:12:53.730
<i>How many Lean Cuisines?</i>

177
00:12:57.910 --> 00:12:58.969
Six.

178
00:12:59.879 --> 00:13:01.347
Six days. then.

179
00:13:03.983 --> 00:13:05.042
What do you want?

180
00:13:06.119 --> 00:13:09.055
We came to tell you
that Will Balint is dead.

181
00:13:10.256 --> 00:13:11.588
Who's Will Balint?

182
00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.688
He's one of the
men who raped you.

183
00:13:22.135 --> 00:13:23.467
Which one?

184
00:13:24.003 --> 00:13:25.232
The taller one.

185
00:13:30.043 --> 00:13:31.136
Okay.

186
00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:47.160
Back already. You must
have really missed me.

187
00:13:47.327 --> 00:13:50.456
Walt wants me to talk to an oil worker
named Archer Loftus. You know him?

188
00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:54.123
Ah. well. I've heard about him. He's
not the most popular guy around here.

189
00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:55.928
No. that would be you.

190
00:13:56.102 --> 00:13:58.469
- What are you talking about?
- Nothing.

191
00:13:58.705 --> 00:14:02.233
Vic. come on. Obviously you're pissed
off about something. something about me.

192
00:14:02.408 --> 00:14:04.604
No. No. I am
pissed off at myself.

193
00:14:04.777 --> 00:14:07.056
'Cause I am so stupid. I thought
you wanted me to call you.

194
00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:08.605
- I did.
- Really?

195
00:14:08.781 --> 00:14:12.047
And who's the girl who answered
the phone when I actually did call?

196
00:14:12.218 --> 00:14:13.311
When did you call?

197
00:14:13.519 --> 00:14:15.647
Jesus. How many are there?

198
00:14:18.391 --> 00:14:19.586
Maddie.

199
00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.629
Who the hell is Maddie?

200
00:14:22.795 --> 00:14:25.822
She's our Ruby. Except she's 22
and she's got a huge crush on me.

201
00:14:25.998 --> 00:14:28.126
Wow! Have you always
suffered from self-esteem issues?

202
00:14:28.701 --> 00:14:30.226
She has told me to
my face five times.

203
00:14:30.403 --> 00:14:32.003
Every time she's had
more than one beer.

204
00:14:33.139 --> 00:14:34.983
What are you two
doing back here?

205
00:14:35.007 --> 00:14:36.805
Looking for Archer Loftus.

206
00:14:38.845 --> 00:14:40.074
So am I.

207
00:14:44.684 --> 00:14:46.550
This is Archer's bunk.

208
00:14:47.687 --> 00:14:50.418
Co-worker reported him
missing just after you all left.

209
00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:53.150
- When's the last time anyone saw him?
- 9:21 a.m.

210
00:14:53.326 --> 00:14:56.888
That was what was on his time
card. Less than an hour into his shift.

211
00:14:57.063 --> 00:14:59.328
- He ever split like this before?
<i>- Nope.</i>

212
00:14:59.665 --> 00:15:01.896
But it was right
after we found Will.

213
00:15:02.135 --> 00:15:04.695
It happens. The guys see
death up close and personal.

214
00:15:04.871 --> 00:15:06.591
brings it home how
dangerous it is out here.

215
00:15:06.739 --> 00:15:08.537
They freak out. they go AWOL.

216
00:15:08.975 --> 00:15:13.504
Shit. As much as I'd like to stick
around and do your job for you.

217
00:15:14.514 --> 00:15:17.211
I'm now two men short and
three hours behind production.

218
00:15:18.885 --> 00:15:20.979
Don't let her take anything.

219
00:15:26.125 --> 00:15:28.822
<i>So. Archer Loftus takes off
right after they find the body.</i>

220
00:15:29.996 --> 00:15:32.056
What is that now.
three coincidences?

221
00:15:36.836 --> 00:15:37.929
So...

222
00:15:38.738 --> 00:15:40.798
Boots. jeans.

223
00:15:40.973 --> 00:15:43.374
A few tools. nothing
too out of the ordinary.

224
00:15:48.714 --> 00:15:50.876
<i>"Cyrano Caballero"?</i>

225
00:15:51.584 --> 00:15:53.246
What is that?

226
00:15:53.419 --> 00:15:55.718
A Big Sky matchmaker
for lonely hearts.

227
00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:59.816
Which is exactly what I need.

228
00:16:01.594 --> 00:16:02.789
What you...

229
00:16:24.851 --> 00:16:27.343
- What's going on with this?
- With what?

230
00:16:28.221 --> 00:16:31.157
You were with me when that
veteran insisted Hector was alive.

231
00:16:31.991 --> 00:16:33.254
<i>Now this.</i>

232
00:16:34.861 --> 00:16:36.454
Hector is dead.
We both know that.

233
00:16:37.597 --> 00:16:39.657
Why does his name
keep coming up?

234
00:16:39.832 --> 00:16:41.392
Why does it never
seem to surprise you?

235
00:16:45.104 --> 00:16:47.300
This is what I look like
when I am surprised.

236
00:16:51.143 --> 00:16:54.443
People are telling stories of
Hector coming back seeking revenge.

237
00:16:54.614 --> 00:16:58.051
This car. for example.
belonged to Jack Mule Deer.

238
00:16:59.585 --> 00:17:03.681
Jack was a drunk with a bad temper
