who knew the identities of the rapists.

481
00:33:21.166 --> 00:33:23.032
It wasn't you. was it?

482
00:33:23.768 --> 00:33:26.169
- No. no.
- Perfect. awesome.

483
00:33:26.338 --> 00:33:28.739
- No. it wasn't me.
- Check that off my list.

484
00:33:31.576 --> 00:33:33.306
- When did it happen?
- Mmm...

485
00:33:34.246 --> 00:33:36.181
Earlier this morning.

486
00:33:39.384 --> 00:33:41.376
- I gotta take this.
- Yeah.

487
00:33:42.554 --> 00:33:43.783
<i>This is Vic.</i>

488
00:33:43.955 --> 00:33:45.446
<i>Victoria. Victoria.</i>

489
00:33:46.458 --> 00:33:49.155
<i>Yeah. Oh. hi. how are you?</i>

490
00:33:49.528 --> 00:33:51.997
Tonight. yeah. No. of
course. yeah. that sounds fun.

491
00:33:52.163 --> 00:33:54.496
Yeah. okay. I'll see you then.

492
00:33:55.534 --> 00:33:57.162
All right. bye.

493
00:33:59.237 --> 00:34:01.172
Who was that?

494
00:34:01.339 --> 00:34:04.867
That was a guy named Archer
Loftus. He's one of our murder suspects.

495
00:34:05.043 --> 00:34:07.376
and I got a date with him.

496
00:34:21.359 --> 00:34:22.588
Eamonn?

497
00:34:24.362 --> 00:34:26.888
Must be important for you
to drive all the way out here.

498
00:34:27.065 --> 00:34:28.829
Yeah. it is.

499
00:34:29.234 --> 00:34:30.759
Unfortunately.

500
00:34:30.936 --> 00:34:33.838
Sheriff Wilkins has ruled
Will Balint's death an accident.

501
00:34:37.275 --> 00:34:38.800
That was quick.

502
00:34:39.578 --> 00:34:42.275
Well. Jim didn't find any
compelling evidence to the contrary.

503
00:34:42.447 --> 00:34:44.848
Plus. he was getting
pressure from Newett Energy

504
00:34:45.016 --> 00:34:46.712
to wrap up the investigation.

505
00:34:47.285 --> 00:34:49.811
Newett Energy happen
to be a campaign donor?

506
00:34:49.988 --> 00:34:51.012
<i>They are.</i>

507
00:34:51.690 --> 00:34:54.888
And they paid for recent department
vehicle and weapon upgrades.

508
00:34:57.596 --> 00:35:01.089
Now. for all we know. this
actually was an accident. but. um...

509
00:35:01.266 --> 00:35:02.325
But what?

510
00:35:04.336 --> 00:35:06.100
You were right to
question that promotion.

511
00:35:07.072 --> 00:35:09.064
I looked at Newett's
employee reviews.

512
00:35:09.240 --> 00:35:12.438
and Will Balint was completely
unqualified for that position.

513
00:35:12.611 --> 00:35:14.409
The promotion should've
gone to Trot Simic.

514
00:35:14.746 --> 00:35:15.975
The guy who found the body.

515
00:35:18.049 --> 00:35:20.280
Archer Loftus have
anything to say about that?

516
00:35:20.518 --> 00:35:22.783
Well. not yet.
we can't find him.

517
00:35:22.954 --> 00:35:25.423
but Vic seems to
think she has a lead.

518
00:35:25.924 --> 00:35:27.984
Where is Vic. anyway?
She's not answering her phone.

519
00:35:28.193 --> 00:35:29.217
I don't know.

520
00:35:29.394 --> 00:35:31.954
Why don't you try her on
her new home number?

521
00:35:33.164 --> 00:35:35.030
I'm sure she'd be
glad to hear from you.

522
00:35:36.234 --> 00:35:38.499
- Here.
- Thanks.

523
00:35:39.371 --> 00:35:40.600
Anyway.

524
00:35:40.772 --> 00:35:43.708
I'm sorry I don't have better
news. but I figured you should know.

525
00:35:44.075 --> 00:35:46.044
- I appreciate it.
- Yeah.

526
00:35:47.345 --> 00:35:48.506
Oh. uh...

527
00:35:48.747 --> 00:35:51.842
Ferg wanted to know if Will
Balint was missing a tooth.

528
00:35:52.117 --> 00:35:53.117
He was.

529
00:35:53.518 --> 00:35:55.118
<i>Must've gotten
knocked out when he fell.</i>

530
00:35:56.588 --> 00:35:58.284
Do you have that autopsy report?

531
00:35:58.456 --> 00:36:00.152
Uh. no. it's not in there.

532
00:36:02.727 --> 00:36:04.093
I probably shouldn't do this.

533
00:36:04.262 --> 00:36:06.231
but I can have the
coroner fax over a copy.

534
00:36:07.532 --> 00:36:09.262
- Thanks. Eamonn.
- Yeah.

535
00:36:16.741 --> 00:36:19.768
I hope you still like fry
bread tacos and catfish pie.

536
00:36:42.600 --> 00:36:45.502
So. Gab. did you ever
try writing to Hector?

537
00:36:48.373 --> 00:36:49.432
Why?

538
00:36:51.042 --> 00:36:52.476
For justice.

539
00:36:53.611 --> 00:36:55.011
<i>There's no Hector.</i>

540
00:36:56.414 --> 00:36:58.144
There's no justice.

541
00:37:00.485 --> 00:37:03.148
- There's just good luck and bad luck.
- That is not true.

542
00:37:03.455 --> 00:37:04.923
Hector lives.

543
00:37:05.890 --> 00:37:07.882
- I promise you.
<i>- Really?</i>

544
00:37:08.460 --> 00:37:10.361
Then why is one of those

545
00:37:10.628 --> 00:37:12.995
men still walking around
like nothing even happened?

546
00:37:19.003 --> 00:37:22.633
Perhaps you could change
this man's luck from good to bad.

547
00:37:30.648 --> 00:37:33.243
Tell Hector what
this man did to you.

548
00:37:35.720 --> 00:37:37.484
And where he can find him.

549
00:37:40.625 --> 00:37:42.651
I'm not leaving the house.

550
00:37:45.263 --> 00:37:46.526
I can't.

551
00:37:47.031 --> 00:37:49.364
I can't.

552
00:37:53.538 --> 00:37:55.439
If you write to Hector.

553
00:37:58.176 --> 00:37:59.838
I will deliver it.

554
00:38:30.608 --> 00:38:31.837
<i>Hector.</i>

555
00:38:32.043 --> 00:38:33.705
<i>I don't know why
I'm writing to you.</i>

556
00:38:35.346 --> 00:38:37.076
<i>Here's what I know.</i>

557
00:38:39.450 --> 00:38:41.351
<i>There were two of them.</i>

558
00:38:42.353 --> 00:38:44.015
<i>One didn't speak.</i>

559
00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:48.357
<i>The other told me to
scream as loud as I wanted</i>

560
00:38:48.526 --> 00:38:50.085
<i>because no one
cares enough to listen.</i>

561
00:38:51.996 --> 00:38:53.464
<i>He was right.</i>

562
00:38:54.966 --> 00:38:56.025
<i>Gab.</i>

563
00:39:27.565 --> 00:39:28.760
Archer!

564
00:39:29.400 --> 00:39:31.335
- Archer. hi!
- Oh. hey.

565
00:39:32.503 --> 00:39:34.096
- You Victoria?
- Yeah.

566
00:39:37.842 --> 00:39:40.744
Oh. look at you.
All right. all right.

567
00:39:41.579 --> 00:39:42.808
Wow!

568
00:39:43.014 --> 00:39:44.774
You're even prettier
than your picture. Whoo!

569
00:39:44.849 --> 00:39:48.308
- What was wrong with my picture?
- Oh. nothing. I wasn't saying that.

570
00:39:48.486 --> 00:39:49.486
I was just saying that...

571
00:39:49.687 --> 00:39:51.781
I should never open my mouth.

572
00:39:51.956 --> 00:39:54.396
It's all right. My daddy always
said that I was too sensitive.

573
00:39:54.459 --> 00:39:56.437
You go ahead and you say
whatever it is you wanna say.

574
00:39:56.461 --> 00:39:58.362
Well. all right.
I do like to talk.

575
00:39:58.529 --> 00:39:59.689
What do you wanna talk about?

576
00:40:00.131 --> 00:40:02.123
Why don't we talk about

577
00:40:02.300 --> 00:40:04.633
why it is that you fled
Newett Energy Oil Field

578
00:40:04.802 --> 00:40:07.328
less than an hour after
a dead body was found?

579
00:40:07.906 --> 00:40:09.397
- Shit moly!
- Shit.

580
00:40:10.341 --> 00:40:11.900
Get out of my way!
Get out of my way!

581
00:40:19.584 --> 00:40:20.677
Hey.

582
00:40:21.152 --> 00:40:23.053
I'm looking for
Henry. Is he around?

583
00:40:23.221 --> 00:40:25.466
Uh... I think I saw him wheel the
mop and bucket to the bathroom.

584
00:40:25.490 --> 00:40:26.651
Thanks.

585
00:40:29.694 --> 00:40:31.890
- We need to talk.
- In here?

586
00:40:32.363 --> 00:40:35.891
Vic just told me that one of
Gab Langton's rapists died.

587
00:40:36.200 --> 00:40:38.431
Under suspicious circumstances.
You hear about that?

588
00:40:40.238 --> 00:40:41.570
Yes.

589
00:40:41.739 --> 00:40:43.708
I was with Walt when
he gave Gab the news.

590
00:40:43.875 --> 00:40:45.366
Oh. okay. Hey.

591
00:40:45.543 --> 00:40:47.034
Piss outside!

592
00:40:48.880 --> 00:40:51.247
Vic also told me that
they're looking for anyone

593
00:40:51.416 --> 00:40:53.817
who might know enough
to target these guys.

594
00:40:54.752 --> 00:40:57.620
I didn't tell them that you came
and asked me to look at their pictures.

595
00:41:05.296 --> 00:41:08.789
Cady. I may not be a lawyer. but I think
I know an accusation when I hear one.

596
00:41:09.000 --> 00:41:11.435
Will Balint died this
morning in the mud.

597
00:41:11.636 --> 00:41:15.368
The same morning that you
came to work late covered in mud.

598
00:41:16.240 --> 00:41:18.209
I'm not an idiot. Henry.

599
00:41:18.676 --> 00:41:20.144
What's going on?

600
00:41:30.388 --> 00:41:32.016
What is going on?

601
00:41:33.324 --> 00:41:36.419
You mean besides the car
trouble I've already told you about?

602
00:41:37.628 --> 00:41:41.793
For one thing. I used to be the proud
owner of a bar I built from scratch.

603
00:41:42.100 --> 00:41:44.592
Now it is owned
by a man I despise.

604
00:41:47.038 --> 00:41:49.769
I barely know who
I am some days.

605
00:41:50.274 --> 00:41:52.607
<i>And I would have thought
that you. of all people.</i>

606
00:41:52.877 --> 00:41:54.903
would understand
how difficult it can be

607
00:41:55.113 --> 00:41:57.241
to have a calling and
not be able to follow it.

608
00:42:05.890 --> 00:42:08.917
Cady. I have too much
respect for what you

609
00:42:09.994 --> 00:42:14.762
and everyone else did to get me out
of jail to risk going back there again.

610
00:42:18.236 --> 00:42:19.704
You're right.

611
00:42:21.639 --> 00:42:23.005
I'm sorry.

612
00:42:45.963 --> 00:42:47.124
<i>So.</i>

613
00:42:47.799 --> 00:42:48.994
<i>Archer.</i>

614
00:42:50.301 --> 00:42:52.930
<i>I take it you're the kind
of worker who calls OSHA</i>

615
00:42:53.171 --> 00:42:54.833
<i>about unsafe work conditions.</i>

616
00:42:56.240 --> 00:43:00.143
But this morning. when one of your
co-workers died on his shift. you...

617
00:43:00.478 --> 00:43:02.276
Well. you didn't call OSHA.

618
00:43:03.114 --> 00:43:04.343
You ran.

619
00:43:05.450 --> 00:43:06.474
Why?

620
00:43:09.587 --> 00:43:12.113
We already know you
clocked out at 9:21 a.m..

621
00:43:13.157 --> 00:43:15.285
just five minutes after
Will Balint was found dead.

622
00:43:16.227 --> 00:43:18.628
<i>And you left without
collecting your things.</i>

623
00:43:19.063 --> 00:43:22.227
And then this evening. when I
showed you my badge. you fled.

624
00:43:22.400 --> 00:43:23.868
Or you tried.

625
00:43:25.136 --> 00:43:27.496
<i>Now. if you don't have an
explanation for all of this.</i>

626
00:43:27.972 --> 00:43:31.534
we're gonna have no choice but to
charge you with Will Balint's murder.

627
00:43:34.545 --> 00:43:37.140
If you did arrest me. how long
could you keep me in custody?

628
00:43:37.348 --> 00:43:38.543
Up to 48 hours.

629
00:43:38.783 --> 00:43:40.513
Here or back in Cumberland?

630
00:43:40.785 --> 00:43:42.253
Well. it could be here.

631
00:43:51.362 --> 00:43:52.796
All right. then arrest me.

632
00:44:02.807 --> 00:44:04.708
Actually. now
that I think of it.

633
00:44:04.976 --> 00:44:07.878
it might be better to release you
into the custody of your employer.

634
00:44:08.045 --> 00:44:09.911
No. I'd prefer to be kept here.

635
00:44:10.314 --> 00:44:11.805
Strongly prefer it. actually.

636
00:44:11.983 --> 00:44:13.503
- Because you killed Will Balint?
- No.

637
00:44:13.584 --> 00:44:15.784
<i>Because you're afraid of
someone at Newett Energy?</i>

638
00:44:21.025 --> 00:44:23.756
Sheriff. if you want an
answer to a question like that.

639
00:44:23.928 --> 00:44:25.920
you've gotta lock
me up in that cell.

640
00:44:26.230 --> 00:44:29.860
And I don't want a Cumberland
County deputy in the room.

641
00:44:43.347 --> 00:44:45.441
Okay. Thank you.

642
00:44:51.422 --> 00:44:54.085
So. I went to work
yesterday. Normal morning.

643
00:44:55.493 --> 00:44:58.327
Then I hear someone yelling
out of the mud pits for help.

644
00:44:58.963 --> 00:45:03.333
By the time I get there. Trot
Simic is giving Will mouth-to-mouth.

645
00:45:03.601 --> 00:45:06.093
But you could
tell it was too late.

646
00:45:06.437 --> 00:45:08.201
He was already dead.

647
00:45:09.373 --> 00:45:12.639
So I kind of freaked
out. and I left.

648
00:45:13.578 --> 00:45:14.910
Why did you get so scared?

649
00:45:15.079 --> 00:45:17.048
<i>Will Balint came
to me last week.</i>

650
00:45:17.248 --> 00:45:20.412
He wanted to know where to go
when you don't feel comfortable

651
00:45:20.585 --> 00:45:22.611
talking to your supervisor.

652
00:45:22.787 --> 00:45:24.119
Who's your supervisor?

653
00:45:26.257 --> 00:45:27.850
Walker Browning.

654
00:45:29.794 --> 00:45:31.023
What'd you tell Will?

655
00:45:31.262 --> 00:45:34.858
<i>Well. I told him to speak to
someone in Human Resources.</i>

656
00:45:35.366 --> 00:45:38.495
The next thing I know. he
gets made all the way up

657
00:45:38.669 --> 00:45:41.696
from roughneck
to assistant driller.

658
00:45:42.607 --> 00:45:45.133
You worked rigs. you know
that just doesn't happen.

659
00:45:45.443 --> 00:45:48.811
<i>So. I figured. hey. they
must have bought Will off.</i>

660
00:45:49.580 --> 00:45:52.550
That is until he got killed. and I
realized what really happened.

661
00:45:55.820 --> 00:45:57.755
They set him up in
order to silence him.

662
00:46:00.491 --> 00:46:02.357
That's quite a conspiracy.

663
00:46:05.529 --> 00:46:07.293
You mean like a
pretty. blonde cop

664
00:46:07.565 --> 00:46:10.467
<i>conspiring to entrap
someone on a dating service?</i>

665
00:46:10.768 --> 00:46:12.532
<i>Yeah. I guess it is.</i>

666
00:46:13.671 --> 00:46:14.934
Crazy me.

667
00:46:16.574 --> 00:46:19.510
Whatever Will told
these guys got him killed.

668
00:46:20.144 --> 00:46:23.512
And. for all I know. they
think I know what Will knew.

669
00:46:23.781 --> 00:46:26.717
So. I got the hell out of there
before they silenced me. too.

670
00:46:27.051 --> 00:46:29.782
Who are you afraid
would try to silence you?

671
00:46:30.054 --> 00:46:31.534
Walker Browning?

672
00:46:31.656 --> 00:46:34.148
Walker doesn't
get his hands dirty.

673
00:46:34.692 --> 00:46:36.024
Who do you think did this. then?

674
00:46:39.096 --> 00:46:40.462
I don't know.

675
00:46:40.765 --> 00:46:44.099
But Walker takes care of
those who take care of him.

676
00:46:45.002 --> 00:46:46.300
Bonuses.

677
00:46:46.671 --> 00:46:48.162
promotions.

678
00:46:48.773 --> 00:46:50.605
<i>I would be willing
to bet. though.</i>

679
00:46:50.808 --> 00:46:55.371
that whoever did kill Will is enjoying
a run of stupid good luck right now.

680
00:47:01.118 --> 00:47:02.245
Whoo!

681
00:47:03.621 --> 00:47:05.920
There he is. There he is.

682
00:47:06.090 --> 00:47:07.558
There you go. gorgeous.

683
00:47:17.268 --> 00:47:19.068
<i>- Are those...
- Take one of those.</i>

684
00:47:22.773 --> 00:47:24.518
<i>- Thank you.
- Squeeze on in there.</i>

685
00:47:24.542 --> 00:47:26.033
Squeeze on in.

686
00:47:26.210 --> 00:47:27.337
There you go.

687
00:47:37.655 --> 00:47:40.921
- No speeding. no drinking. Understood?
- Gotcha.

688
00:47:41.092 --> 00:47:42.602
Don't stop until you
get to the reservation.

689
00:47:42.626 --> 00:47:44.219
- Yes. sir. Mr. Browning.
- All right.

690
00:47:46.597 --> 00:47:47.997
<i>Be careful tonight. fellas.</i>

691
00:47:48.265 --> 00:47:50.564
These ladies look
awful frisky to me.

692
00:47:50.735 --> 00:47:52.295
Yeah! MAN 2:
<i>Here's to you. boss.</i>

693
00:47:52.436 --> 00:47:54.701
<i>- You know it. boss.
- Have fun. All right?</i>

694
00:47:54.872 --> 00:47:56.568
<i>Yeah.</i> WOMAN: Yeah.

695
00:48:05.583 --> 00:48:07.176
Looks like some lucky guys.

696
00:48:07.485 --> 00:48:08.783
I don't know.

697
00:48:09.019 --> 00:48:11.250
Right place at the right time.

698
00:48:12.857 --> 00:48:14.018
Is that really luck?

699
00:48:15.993 --> 00:48:17.017
I suppose not.

700
00:48:24.769 --> 00:48:27.705
So. putting up that dating
profile to find Archer...

701
00:48:27.872 --> 00:48:28.872
He's right.

702
00:48:29.540 --> 00:48:31.839
That might be
considered entrapment.

703
00:48:32.009 --> 00:48:34.001
Please. He was just thanking me.

704
00:48:34.178 --> 00:48:37.637
I have never seen anyone so
excited to get locked up before.

705
00:48:38.449 --> 00:48:41.749
He's clearly scared
shitless of Walker Browning.

706
00:48:42.153 --> 00:48:43.746
He doesn't trust Eamonn.

707
00:48:44.155 --> 00:48:46.989
Maybe he just doesn't
trust Eamonn's boss.

708
00:48:47.725 --> 00:48:50.160
Apparently. Newett
Energy urged Sheriff Wilkins

709
00:48:50.327 --> 00:48:53.525
to rule the death an
accident. which is strange.

710
00:48:53.864 --> 00:48:54.864
Why?

711
00:48:55.232 --> 00:48:58.964
Because a workplace accident opens up
the company to a big OSHA investigation.

712
00:48:59.837 --> 00:49:02.534
Wrongful death
lawsuits. hefty fines.

713
00:49:03.407 --> 00:49:06.639
But a simple murder is
outside of the company's liability.

714
00:49:06.811 --> 00:49:08.712
They're free and clear.

715
00:49:10.314 --> 00:49:12.579
So why insist on
ruling it an accident?

716
00:49:12.817 --> 00:49:15.082
Unless you're trying
to cover up a murder.

717
00:49:15.486 --> 00:49:18.149
Finally got Will Balint's
autopsy to print out.

718
00:49:18.322 --> 00:49:20.314
How old is that fax
machine. exactly?

719
00:49:21.492 --> 00:49:24.951
An autopsy report just made
a two-hour trip in seconds.

720
00:49:25.129 --> 00:49:26.859
That's pretty good.

721
00:49:28.232 --> 00:49:29.232
Huh.

722
00:49:30.034 --> 00:49:32.868
What is it? Something to
do with that missing tooth?

723
00:49:34.638 --> 00:49:37.369
No. No. it's something else.

724
00:49:39.410 --> 00:49:41.777
Shall we beg you to tell us?

725
00:49:43.914 --> 00:49:45.439
- Mud.
- Great.

726
00:49:46.083 --> 00:49:47.449
That clears it up.

727
00:49:47.751 --> 00:49:52.348
There was mud in Will Balint's
esophagus and his stomach.

728
00:49:54.225 --> 00:49:55.955
Well. that doesn't
happen if he suffocated.

729
00:49:56.327 --> 00:49:58.125
No. No. it doesn't.

730
00:49:59.263 --> 00:50:02.461
If he inhaled mud. that
means he was conscious. so

731
00:50:03.067 --> 00:50:04.695
he had his face in the mud.

732
00:50:04.869 --> 00:50:07.202
someone was pushing him.
and he was trying to fight back.

733
00:50:08.072 --> 00:50:09.506
So much for a drilling accident.

734
00:50:09.673 --> 00:50:11.938
I also found out who got
promoted after Will died.

735
00:50:12.376 --> 00:50:14.038
- Trot Simic.
<i>- Yeah.</i>

736
00:50:14.578 --> 00:50:16.308
That sounds like a
run of stupid good luck.

737
00:50:16.547 --> 00:50:19.745
- He also get a bonus?
- If he did. he's out spending it now.

738
00:50:20.017 --> 00:50:22.486
Apparently. he went out to
celebrate his promotion tonight.

739
00:50:22.653 --> 00:50:24.815
so we'll have to wait for
tomorrow to talk to him.

740
00:50:26.190 --> 00:50:27.190
Maybe not.

741
00:50:28.893 --> 00:50:32.193
I think I may know where
he's celebrating. Let's go.

742
00:50:43.974 --> 00:50:45.704
Put it away. Heflin.

743
00:50:46.110 --> 00:50:48.306
- This one's on me.
- The last one was on you.

744
00:50:48.879 --> 00:50:50.108
Well...

745
00:50:51.982 --> 00:50:53.075
Look. I owe you one.

746
00:50:53.951 --> 00:50:57.251
I should. uh. be making
things easier for you.

747
00:50:59.023 --> 00:51:01.993
Not making you feel like you've
gotta tiptoe around my ego.

748
00:51:02.159 --> 00:51:04.993
No. no. no. it's cool. I...

749
00:51:05.329 --> 00:51:07.924
I get it. You guys
are like a family.

750
00:51:08.599 --> 00:51:10.033
A small. dysfunctional family.

751
00:51:11.602 --> 00:51:15.437
I know it can't be easy trying to figure
out how to fit someone new into that.

752
00:51:17.041 --> 00:51:18.202
All right. man.

753
00:51:18.542 --> 00:51:19.908
Oh.

754
00:51:21.178 --> 00:51:22.578
One second.

755
00:51:23.814 --> 00:51:24.814
Hey. Ruby.

756
00:51:25.015 --> 00:51:27.143
- Where are you?
<i>- Oh. uh. Sheriff.</i>

757
00:51:27.318 --> 00:51:29.981
Uh... Sorry. I'm
at the Red Pony.

758
00:51:30.254 --> 00:51:31.381
You been drinking?

759
00:51:32.890 --> 00:51:34.085
A little.

760
00:51:34.625 --> 00:51:35.684
Okay.

761
00:51:35.960 --> 00:51:37.053
What? Uh...

762
00:51:42.099 --> 00:51:44.034
- Over it.
- We're over it.

763
00:51:47.104 --> 00:51:48.504
Hello? Yeah.

764
00:51:49.373 --> 00:51:52.241
No. no. just a couple
of non-alcoholic beers.

765
00:51:52.409 --> 00:51:54.605
I don't actually drink. so...

766
00:51:55.479 --> 00:51:57.209
Casino?

767
00:51:58.215 --> 00:51:59.376
All right.

768
00:51:59.617 --> 00:52:01.483
Okay. who am I looking for?

769
00:52:01.719 --> 00:52:03.415
Trot Simic. Okay.

770
00:52:04.254 --> 00:52:06.189
All right. I'll be right there.

771
00:52:06.457 --> 00:52:07.823
Sorry. man.

772
00:52:24.375 --> 00:52:25.399
<i>No. no. no.</i>

773
00:52:25.643 --> 00:52:26.770
<i>Tell him. tell him.</i>

774
00:52:29.179 --> 00:52:30.619
<i>- All right.</i>
- Who needs a beer?

775
00:52:31.148 --> 00:52:33.481
<i>- Thank you.
- Who needs a beer?</i>

776
00:52:33.651 --> 00:52:35.451
<i>You need a cigarette.
don't you? There you go.</i>

777
00:52:37.287 --> 00:52:38.527
<i>- There you go.
- No. no.</i>

778
00:52:38.622 --> 00:52:40.147
<i>You got one?</i>

779
00:52:42.493 --> 00:52:44.485
Are you doing all right?

780
00:52:46.296 --> 00:52:48.424
- I'm looking at the stars.
- Oh.

781
00:52:50.534 --> 00:52:51.695
The Pleiades.

782
00:52:53.704 --> 00:52:54.933
Yeah. yeah.

783
00:52:55.172 --> 00:52:59.007
My grandma used to tell me the legends
of their mother and her seven pups.

784
00:53:01.145 --> 00:53:04.206
Well. you know. there's a
clearing back in the woods a way.

785
00:53:04.415 --> 00:53:06.680
You can see the
whole sky from there.

786
00:53:06.917 --> 00:53:10.046
You wanna grab these
beers and go over there

787
00:53:11.088 --> 00:53:12.386
and tell me the story?

788
00:53:18.996 --> 00:53:20.396
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

789
00:53:21.799 --> 00:53:23.165
All right.

790
00:53:26.804 --> 00:53:29.467
I think we're crossing about
five jurisdictional lines right now.

791
00:53:29.740 --> 00:53:31.299
You learn to get used to it.

792
00:53:31.508 --> 00:53:35.240
Let's just focus on taking Trot
Simic into custody if he's here.

793
00:53:35.512 --> 00:53:37.879
We'll sort out
the details later.

794
00:53:40.918 --> 00:53:43.581
How much further until
we reach the clearing?

795
00:53:43.887 --> 00:53:45.913
Well. we're already here.

796
00:53:48.425 --> 00:53:49.620
We are?

797
00:53:52.129 --> 00:53:54.257
There you go. There you go.

798
00:53:54.431 --> 00:53:56.866
<i>Come on. a little
dancing. Come on now.</i>

799
00:53:57.101 --> 00:53:59.021
Everybody. stop where you are. -

800
00:53:59.169 --> 00:54:00.296
put your hands in the air.

801
00:54:04.975 --> 00:54:06.102
This is bullshit.

802
00:54:07.010 --> 00:54:10.208
- You've got no authority here...
- Put your hands in the air now.

803
00:54:14.585 --> 00:54:16.952
Congratulations on
your big promotion. Trot.

804
00:54:19.056 --> 00:54:21.150
Too bad Will's not here
to celebrate with you.

805
00:54:25.095 --> 00:54:28.031
Maybe we ought to
move things to the station.

806
00:54:28.766 --> 00:54:30.064
talk about why that is.

807
00:54:33.570 --> 00:54:35.402
Stop it. What are you doing?

808
00:54:35.572 --> 00:54:36.692
What do you think I'm doing?

809
00:54:36.840 --> 00:54:37.899
No!

810
00:54:38.142 --> 00:54:39.201
Hey. hey.

811
00:54:49.753 --> 00:54:50.982
Whoa. whoa. whoa.

812
00:54:51.388 --> 00:54:54.517
I'll get off her. just
leave me alone. all right?

813
00:54:55.459 --> 00:54:57.121
Scream all you want.

814
00:55:02.099 --> 00:55:04.193
No one will care
enough to listen.

815
00:55:10.374 --> 00:55:13.742
If you ever step foot on this
land again to hurt another woman.

816
00:55:13.977 --> 00:55:15.445
I won't just take your teeth.

817
00:55:15.913 --> 00:55:16.972
I'll take your life.

818
00:55:26.623 --> 00:55:27.903
- Did you hear that?
- Stay here.

819
00:55:34.264 --> 00:55:35.264
Gab?

820
00:55:35.933 --> 00:55:38.368
<i>Gab. we have to run.</i>

821
00:55:39.636 --> 00:55:41.298
I'm sure someone
heard the gunshot.

822
00:55:41.538 --> 00:55:42.631
We have to run.

823
00:55:45.242 --> 00:55:46.301
Gab.

824
00:55:46.977 --> 00:55:47.977
Run.

825
00:55:59.857 --> 00:56:01.416
Give me the gun.

826
00:56:02.259 --> 00:56:03.283
I dropped it back there.

827
00:56:05.729 --> 00:56:06.890
Go.

828
00:56:19.576 --> 00:56:21.340
Sheriff's Department!

829
00:56:22.779 --> 00:56:23.906
Stop!

830
00:56:25.015 --> 00:56:26.745
Stop or I'll shoot!

831
00:57:29.279 --> 00:57:30.279
English -SDH
